I'm a little bit late for the 30 October 2023 deadline, but I support this,
unsurprisingly. :-)

On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 at 10:32=E2=80=AFAM Bas Westerbaan <bas=3D
40cloudflare.com@dmarc.ietf.org> wrote:

> Yes, please.
>
> On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 at 3:55=E2=80=AFPM Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com> wrot=
e:
>
>> Hi! After a request from and discussions with the authors of
>> draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids [1], the chairs would like to determine
>> whether there is consensus to request an early code point assignment; se=
e
>> [2] about the early allocation process. The code point in question is fo=
r
>> 'trust_anchors' in the TLS ExtensionType Values registry, see Section 12=
.1
>> of the I-D. As noted in [3], implementers have been using a value chosen=
 at
>> random and it has been stable since the initial draft. Please let the li=
st
>> know by 30 October 2023 if you support this early allocation.
>>
>> NOTE: A new registry is defined in Section 12.3 of the I-D, but we canno=
t
>> ask for early creation of a registry.
>>
>> Cheers,
>> spt (for the chairs)
>>
>> [1] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/
>> [2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc7120/
>> [3]
>> https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/tls/vD37D986i5YtFFvfLfkcte_WSxk/
>> _______________________________________________
>> TLS mailing list -- tls@ietf.org
>> To unsubscribe send an email to tls-leave@ietf.org
>>
